{
  "acceptance_gates": {
    "accuracy_target_millihartree": 1.6,
    "binding_arm_rule": "max over the declared mapping arms. A candidate passes only if its widest arm fits; the reduced +2q arms have been strictly smaller on every committed instance, but that is an observation, not a guarantee, so the maximum is taken rather than assumed.",
    "margin_factor": 3.0,
    "margin_factor_basis": "The shot-search pass rule bounds replica RMSE against the exact reference, and RMSE combines bank bias with sampling scatter in quadrature. A bank sitting at the target has no allowance left for shot noise at any endpoint, so the margin exists to reserve the target for the statistical component. At margin 3 the bias takes 0.533 mHa, which is (1/3)^2 = 11.1 percent of the MSE budget, and the statistical RMSE allowance falls from 1.6 to 1.5085 mHa -- a 5.7 percent reduction. Those are two different fractions and the smaller one is not a share of a shot budget consumed. Note what this argument does and does not do: it motivates having a margin, and it does not pick 3 out of 2 or 5. See margin_factor_status.",
    "margin_factor_status": "declared_here_not_preregistered",
    "margin_factor_status_basis": "This config and the first result it produces enter the repository in the same commit, so factor 3 is not preregistered with respect to this run and the LiH admission is exploratory evidence for the rule rather than a test of it. Recording that plainly is cheaper than the alternative, which would be to claim a preregistration the history does not support. Two things limit the damage. Every candidate's margin_sensitivity records the range of margin factors over which its verdict is unchanged, re-derived from the walked rows, so a reader can see whether the verdict turns on the number at all. And the rule is frozen from this commit onward: the preregistered use is the next candidate screened under it.",
    "screen_authorizes_a_probe_not_a_price": true,
    "selection_may_not_use_mapping_cost_direction": true,
    "word_universe_ceiling": 2048,
    "word_universe_ceiling_basis": "Carried forward in intent from the QR3b preregistration: BeH2 is the only bank that has ever priced inside this grid, at W=1814 on its full-width arms, and the ceiling is the next power of two above it. This is an operational admission threshold calibrated on one success, not a demonstrated necessary condition for priceability -- coefficient magnitudes, grouping, estimator variance and pencil conditioning all bear on whether a bank resolves, and W is a proxy for the reconstruction variance the shot search has to overcome rather than that variance itself. What supports it is that both banks rejected so far, h4_converged at W=7926 and LiH at its intrinsic stop at W=7740, sit about four times above it.",
    "word_universe_convention": "non_identity_words_only",
    "word_universe_convention_basis": "The tree carries two conventions differing by one: mapping_axis counts the identity word (BeH2 full-width 1815), protocol_axis and the QR3b probe do not (1814). The ceiling was calibrated in the second, and the identity is the one word a shot budget never buys -- its expectation is fixed by normalization -- so it contributes nothing to the reconstruction variance the ceiling stands in for. The screen counts as protocol_axis does, and check_priceability_screen.py calibrates against that record rather than mapping_axis."
  },
